ulfac-s: n!, for n from 0 to 9, in two parts: the thousands and the last three digits.
Cells 65-98. To call it, load n into the accumulator and JMP 65.
It returns the last three digits of n! in the accumulator and its thousands in cell 94.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99.
Size 34 cells. It runs at most 11 instructions, 11.0 on average, counted from cell 65 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain; outside it, n reads past the tables.

